course: dictionary
lesson: 5664
title: Litmus: the colour-changing test
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Litmus is a special dye that changes colour to show what kind of liquid it touches. You can use the words around it as clues. «Litmus paper turns red in acid and blue in alkali.» The colour changes are the clue: the paper changes colour, so it is testing the liquid.
explain: In science lessons, you dip a strip of litmus paper into a liquid. Lemon juice turns it red, so lemon juice is an acid. Soap water turns it blue, so soap water is an alkali. Pure water causes no change, so it is neutral.
explain: Litmus also has a meaning beyond the lab. «A litmus test» is a simple test that shows what something is really like. If a leader's answer to one key question shows the truth, people can call that question a litmus test. Ask yourself: does the word fit a test that shows the truth?
fact: Litmus is a dye, a colour that can change.
fact: «Litmus paper, made from lichens, turns red in acid and blue in alkali.»
fact: Acids turn litmus paper red, and alkalis turn it blue.
fact: Pure water does not change litmus paper, because it is neutral.
fact: A «litmus test» can also mean one simple question that shows the truth.
exercise: «Litmus paper turns red in acid and blue in alkali.» What colour does litmus paper turn in acid? | *Red | Green | Yellow | Blue
exercise: Scientists use indicators too: litmus paper, made from lichens, turns red in acid and blue in alkali. What is litmus paper made from? | Soap water | Lemon juice | *Lichens | Coal
exercise: Sofia says a litmus test needs a tube and a flame. What does litmus test mean in everyday talk? | A test for how tall you are | A long exam with many questions | *One simple question that shows the truth | A test done with a flame
test: «Soap water turns litmus paper blue.» What kind of liquid is soap water? | Acid | Red litmus | *Alkali | Lichen
test: «The vote was a litmus test for the new leader.» What does litmus test mean here? | A test done with a flame | A long essay | *A simple test that shows what the leader is really like | A type of soap
exam: «Lemon juice turns litmus paper red.» What does this tell a scientist? | It is a dye made from fish | It is neutral | *It is an acid | It is an alkali
